* [105]On \(B\) sublattice \(S_{i}\rightarrow-S_{i}\). Under this transformation the spin part of the \(\phi_{ji}\) in Eq. (39) can be written as:

\[\frac{\left(S-S_{i}^{z}\right)\left(S-S_{j}^{z}\right)+S_{i}^{-}S_{j}^{+}}{ \left(S-S_{i}^{z}\right)\left(S-S_{j}^{z}\right)+S_{j}^{-}S_{i}^{+}}\] \[=\frac{\left(S+S_{i}^{z}\right)\left(S+S_{j}^{z}\right)+S_{j}^{-}S_ {i}^{+}}{\left(S+S_{i}^{z}\right)\left(S+S_{j}^{z}\right)+S_{i}^{-}S_{j}^{+}} \cdot\frac{S_{j}^{+}S_{i}^{-}}{S_{i}^{z}S_{j}^{-}}.\]* [106]\(\mathcal{H}(\vec{k})\) is a 2\(\times\)2 matrix. In terms of _Pauli matrices_ it is represented as

\[\mathcal{H}(\vec{k})=\mathcal{H}_{0}\mathcal{I}+\mathcal{H}_{x}( \vec{k})\sigma_{x}+\mathcal{H}_{y}(\vec{k})\sigma_{y}+\mathcal{H}_{\xi}(\vec{k })\sigma_{z},\] where, \[\mathcal{H}_{0}(\vec{k})=\frac{H_{i,j\in A}+H_{i,j\in B}}{2}, \mathcal{H}_{x}(\vec{k})=\mathrm{Re}\left[H_{i\in A,j\in B}\right],\] \[\mathcal{H}_{z}(\vec{k})=\frac{H_{i,j\in A}-H_{i,j\in B}}{2}, \mathcal{H}_{y}(\vec{k})=\mathrm{Im}\left[H_{i\in A,j\in B}\right].\] Here, \(\mathcal{I}\) is the \(2\times 2\) unit matrix; \(\sigma_{x}\), \(\sigma_{y}\), and \(\sigma_{z}\) are the Pauli matrices.
